NAME
    ssh-askpass - OpenSSH askpass companion for ssh.lib.sh

SYNOPSIS
    ssh-askpass prompt

DESCRIPTION
    ssh-askpass is the bootstrap-integrated helper used by ssh_auth and
    ssh_password.

    OpenSSH invokes the helper with one prompt operand.

    For ssh_auth, the helper reads one copy of the invocation-owned reusable
    secret from m_SSH_ASKPASS_FIFO. Multiple helper invocations during the same
    OpenSSH authentication attempt may therefore receive the same secret.

    For ssh_password, the helper consumes the invocation-owned one-shot IPC
    value identified by m_SSH_ASKPASS_ID.

    Exactly one provider must be selected.

    When OpenSSH marks the request as a confirmation prompt through
    SSH_ASKPASS_PROMPT=confirm, ssh-askpass refuses the request before reading
    either provider.

    Normal callers use ssh_auth or ssh_password from ssh.lib.sh rather than
    invoking this command directly.

ENVIRONMENT
    m_SSH_ASKPASS_FIFO
        Private FIFO established by ssh_auth for repeatable secret delivery.

    m_SSH_ASKPASS_ID
        One-shot IPC identity established by ssh_password.

    SSH_ASKPASS_PROMPT
        OpenSSH prompt classification. The value confirm is refused.

EXIT STATUS
    0   authentication secret delivered successfully
    1   confirmation request, invalid provider selection, invalid provider
        resource, or provider read failure
    2   invocation does not contain exactly one prompt operand

SEE ALSO
    ssh.lib.sh
    ipc.lib.sh
